<!-- ===================== 7. SCOPE ===================== -->
<h1>7. Scope of the Application</h1>

<h2>7.1 In scope</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th style="width:28%">Area</th><th>Included</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Employee management</td><td>List, add and delete employees; validation of name, position, company e-mail, +63 contact number and salary (2 decimals, range per position); unique e-mail addresses; all errors shown at once, each under its field; generated employee codes; sample data.</td></tr>
  <tr class="alt"><td>Payroll processing</td><td>Monthly payroll run per employee with overtime, SSS, PhilHealth, Pag-IBIG, BIR withholding tax and other deductions; one run per employee per month; saved history.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Payslips and exports</td><td>On-screen itemised breakdown, payslip viewer, JSON download in the app, and a CSV export endpoint.</td></tr>
  <tr class="alt"><td>Employee photos</td><td>Upload, replace, display and delete in a private S3 bucket with expiring links.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>AI review</td><td>Fixed rules plus OpenAI review of payroll records with a reason for each.</td></tr>
  <tr class="alt"><td>AI chat</td><td>A chat assistant limited by instruction to answering from current employee and payroll data.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Sign-in and access control</td><td>Sign in, sign up, forgot and reset password; accounts with the roles <i>admin</i> and <i>member</i>; signed JWT tokens valid for 60 minutes, verified by each service on its own; admins manage employees, payroll and photos while members have read-only access plus AI review and chat; five failed attempts lock an account for 15 minutes; checked by all three services. A first administrator is created at start-up.</td></tr>
  <tr class="alt"><td>User interface</td><td>Web app with sign-in screens, directory, payroll form, history, payslip viewer and chat widget, with controls shown according to role.</td></tr>
  <tr class="alt"><td>Operations</td><td>Health endpoints, AWS status check, and clear startup messages showing AWS and key configuration.</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>7.2 Out of scope (not built)</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Persistent user accounts (accounts live in memory and are lost on restart), e-mail confirmation at sign-up, sending the reset code by e-mail, changing a password while signed in, an admin screen to manage users or change roles, and an external identity provider.</li>
  <li>HTTPS (traffic is plain HTTP on the local machine).</li>
  <li>Editing an existing employee; a persistent employee database.</li>
  <li>Attendance, leave, loans, 13th-month pay, holiday or night-differential pay, and semi-monthly pay periods.</li>
  <li>Bulk payroll for all employees at once, approval workflows, and bank payment files.</li>
  <li>Official government forms and reports (BIR, SSS, PhilHealth, Pag-IBIG).</li>
  <li>PDF payslips and e-mail delivery.</li>
  <li>Production deployment, containers, monitoring and automated build pipelines.</li>
  <li>Automated test suites beyond a single application start-up test.</li>
</ul>

<!-- ===================== 8. FUTURE ENHANCEMENTS ===================== -->
<h1>8. Future Enhancements</h1>
<p>Grouped by area. Priority reflects the value gained relative to the effort and risk of leaving the gap open.</p>

<table>
  <tr><th style="width:15%">Area</th><th>Enhancement</th><th>Benefit</th><th style="width:10%">Priority</th></tr>
  <tr><td rowspan="8"><b>Security</b></td><td>Keep users in the persistent database; require a strong password for the seeded administrator (it is currently the short password <span class="code">admin</span>).</td><td>Accounts survive restarts; no weak default credential.</td><td>High</td></tr>
  <tr class="alt"><td>HTTPS everywhere and a secrets manager for the JWT secret, API keys and credentials.</td><td>Tokens and passwords protected in transit; no secrets in files.</td><td>High</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Make tokens cancellable: keep a short list of revoked tokens that every service checks, or use a much shorter lifetime with refresh tokens.</td><td>Sign-out, password reset and role changes take effect at once instead of when the token expires.</td><td>High</td></tr>
  <tr class="alt"><td>Move from one shared secret to asymmetric signing (RS256/ES256): employee-service keeps a private key and publishes the public key; the other services verify with the public key only.</td><td>The other services can no longer forge tokens even if one of them is compromised; secrets are not copied between services.</td><td>Medium</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Send reset codes by e-mail (today the code is written to the server log) and confirm e-mail addresses at sign-up.</td><td>A usable reset flow; stops anyone creating an account with an address they do not own.</td><td>High</td></tr>
  <tr class="alt"><td>An admin screen to manage users and roles; change password while signed in; optional move to an external identity provider (OIDC) with signed tokens.</td><td>Complete account management; sign-in no longer depends on one service being up.</td><td>Medium</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Rate limiting and usage caps on the AI endpoints.</td><td>Controls OpenAI cost and abuse.</td><td>Medium</td></tr>
  <tr class="alt"><td>Audit log of who created, changed or deleted records.</td><td>Accountability for payroll data.</td><td>Medium</td></tr>

  <tr><td rowspan="4"><b>Data</b></td><td>Replace H2 with a persistent database such as PostgreSQL, with managed migrations.</td><td>Employee data survives restarts; stable IDs.</td><td>High</td></tr>
  <tr class="alt"><td>Move payroll history from a JSON file to the database.</td><td>Safe concurrent access, queries, multi-instance deployment.</td><td>High</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Stable employee identity that photos and payroll runs reference; soft delete. (A unique e-mail constraint already exists.)</td><td>Removes the risk of old runs or photos pointing to the wrong person.</td><td>High</td></tr>
  <tr class="alt"><td>Make SSS, PhilHealth, Pag-IBIG and tax tables configurable with effective dates.</td><td>Rate changes without code changes; correct history.</td><td>High</td></tr>

  <tr><td rowspan="5"><b>Payroll features</b></td><td>Edit employee records.</td><td>Complete employee management.</td><td>Medium</td></tr>
  <tr class="alt"><td>Run payroll for all employees at once, with an approval step.</td><td>Matches how payroll is actually run.</td><td>Medium</td></tr>
  <tr><td>13th-month pay, holiday and night differentials, leave and attendance integration, semi-monthly periods.</td><td>Covers Philippine payroll practice more fully.</td><td>Medium</td></tr>
  <tr class="alt"><td>PDF payslips, e-mail delivery, and government remittance reports.</td><td>Deliverables employees and agencies expect.</td><td>Medium</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Payroll history filters, search and CSV download from the UI.</td><td>Easier reporting.</td><td>Low</td></tr>

  <tr class="alt"><td rowspan="4"><b>AI</b></td><td>Automated tests that confirm the chat refuses off-topic and prompt-injection questions.</td><td>Evidence that the data-only rule holds.</td><td>High</td></tr>
  <tr class="alt"><td>Redact personal details before sending to OpenAI, or offer a self-hosted or offline model option.</td><td>Better privacy for real employee data.</td><td>High</td></tr>
  <tr class="alt"><td>Cite the records used in each chat answer; add retrieval for larger datasets.</td><td>Traceable answers that scale.</td><td>Medium</td></tr>
  <tr class="alt"><td>Compare each employee with their own history; cache repeated reviews.</td><td>More meaningful flags, lower cost.</td><td>Low</td></tr>

  <tr><td rowspan="5"><b>Quality and operations</b></td><td>Unit, integration and contract tests for all three services and the UI.</td><td>Safer changes; catches regressions.</td><td>High</td></tr>
  <tr class="alt"><td>Docker Compose to start every component with one command.</td><td>Repeatable setup.</td><td>Medium</td></tr>
  <tr><td>CI/CD pipeline running build, lint and tests.</td><td>Automatic quality gate.</td><td>Medium</td></tr>
  <tr class="alt"><td>API gateway, centralised logging, health monitoring and OpenAPI documentation for all services.</td><td>Operational visibility and consistent docs.</td><td>Medium</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Split the front end into components and services; adopt TypeScript; accessibility and mobile review.</td><td>Maintainability and usability.</td><td>Low</td></tr>
</table>

<!-- ===================== 9. ASSUMPTIONS AND LIMITATIONS ===================== -->
<h1>9. Assumptions and Known Limitations</h1>
<table>
  <tr><th style="width:28%">Item</th><th>Detail</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Employee data is in memory</td><td>employee-service resets to the 10 sample employees on every restart and employee IDs restart at 1. Payroll runs and S3 photos keep the old IDs, so they can end up referring to a different person.</td></tr>
  <tr class="alt"><td>Accounts are in memory</td><td>Accounts created by sign-up and reset codes disappear when employee-service restarts. Only the seeded administrator (<span class="code">vance.albert.reyes@pwc.com</span>) is recreated. The lock-out counters are also in memory. A token issued before a restart still works until it expires, even if its account is gone.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Tokens cannot be cancelled</td><td>A JWT is not stored on the server, so signing out only clears the browser, and a password reset or role change does not affect tokens already issued. Each works until its 60 minutes are up, so a copied token can be used until then.</td></tr>
  <tr class="alt"><td>One shared secret</td><td><span class="code">JWT_SECRET</span> signs and verifies every token and must be identical in all three services. Anyone who learns it can forge an admin token. Keep it out of source control (all three <span class="code">.env</span> files are git-ignored; the <span class="code">.env.example</span> files must stay empty) and change it if it leaks, which signs everyone out. If the values differ, sign-in succeeds but the other two services answer 401.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Weak seeded admin password</td><td>The administrator's starting password is <span class="code">admin</span>, shorter than the 8-character minimum required of new passwords. Change it before real use. A password reset requires at least 8 characters.</td></tr>
  <tr class="alt"><td>Forgot password has no e-mail</td><td>The reset code is written to the employee-service log. Anyone who can read that log can reset a password. A real deployment must send it by e-mail.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Open sign-up</td><td>Anyone with a <span class="code">@pwc.com</span> address can create a member account, without e-mail confirmation. Members cannot change data.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Sign-in depends on employee-service</td><td>Nobody can sign in while it is down. Users who already hold a valid token can still use payroll-service and ai-service, because those verify tokens themselves; only calls that need employee data fail (502). Traffic is plain HTTP, so tokens could be read on a real network.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Statutory rates are demonstration values</td><td>SSS, PhilHealth, Pag-IBIG and BIR figures must be verified against official sources before real use.</td></tr>
  <tr class="alt"><td>Data leaves the machine for AI</td><td>The review sends salary figures only. The chat also sends employee names, e-mail addresses, contact numbers and salaries to OpenAI. Confirm this is acceptable for the data being used.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Chat scope is instruction-based</td><td>The restriction to on-topic, data-only answers is enforced by model instructions, not code. It is strong with <span class="code">temperature=0</span> but not an absolute guarantee. The AI review is advisory; a person decides what to do with a flagged record.</td></tr>
  <tr class="alt"><td>Review threshold interaction</td><td>Since tax and contributions are now part of deductions, higher salaries can exceed the "20% of gross" rule and be marked for review. The threshold may need raising.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Single-instance file storage</td><td>payroll-runs.json suits one running copy of payroll-service. Malformed JSON in a request currently produces a 500 rather than a 400.</td></tr>
  <tr class="alt"><td>Testing status</td><td>The only automated test checks that employee-service starts. Features have been checked by hand by running the app (including the employee validation, unique e-mail and per-field errors), but there are no automated unit, API or UI tests, so changes need a manual regression pass before release.</td></tr>
</table>

<!-- ===================== APPENDIX ===================== -->
<h1>Appendix A. API Endpoint Summary</h1>

<p>Unless marked <i>open</i>, every endpoint needs the JWT from sign-in in the header <span class="code">Authorization: Bearer &lt;token&gt;</span>. <i>Admin</i> means the token's role claim must be admin (403 otherwise). A missing, forged, tampered or expired token gives 401.</p>

<h2>employee-service (port 8081)</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th style="width:12%">Method</th><th style="width:30%">Path</th><th>Purpose</th><th style="width:12%">Access</th><th style="width:20%">Responses</th></tr>
  <tr><td>GET</td><td><span class="code">/api/employees</span></td><td>List all employees</td><td>signed in</td><td>200, 401</td></tr>
  <tr class="alt"><td>GET</td><td><span class="code">/api/employees/{id}</span></td><td>Get one employee</td><td>signed in</td><td>200, 401, 404</td></tr>
  <tr><td>POST</td><td><span class="code">/api/employees</span></td><td>Add an employee</td><td>admin</td><td>201, 400, 401, 403, 409</td></tr>
  <tr class="alt"><td>DELETE</td><td><span class="code">/api/employees/{id}</span></td><td>Delete an employee</td><td>admin</td><td>204, 401, 403, 404</td></tr>
  <tr><td>POST</td><td><span class="code">/api/auth/signup</span></td><td>Create a member account and sign in</td><td>open</td><td>201, 400, 409</td></tr>
  <tr class="alt"><td>POST</td><td><span class="code">/api/auth/login</span></td><td>Sign in; returns a JWT, its expiry and the user</td><td>open</td><td>200, 400, 401, 429</td></tr>
  <tr><td>POST</td><td><span class="code">/api/auth/forgot-password</span></td><td>Create a reset code (written to the server log); same answer whether or not the account exists</td><td>open</td><td>200, 400</td></tr>
  <tr class="alt"><td>POST</td><td><span class="code">/api/auth/reset-password</span></td><td>Set a new password with the reset code</td><td>open</td><td>200, 400, 429</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>payroll-service (port 3001)</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th style="width:12%">Method</th><th style="width:30%">Path</th><th>Purpose</th><th style="width:12%">Access</th><th style="width:20%">Responses</th></tr>
  <tr><td>GET</td><td><span class="code">/health</span></td><td>Liveness check</td><td>open</td><td>200</td></tr>
  <tr class="alt"><td>GET</td><td><span class="code">/api/payroll</span></td><td>List saved payroll runs</td><td>signed in</td><td>200, 401, 502</td></tr>
  <tr><td>POST</td><td><span class="code">/api/payroll/run</span></td><td>Calculate and save a payroll run</td><td>admin</td><td>201, 400, 401, 403, 404, 409, 502</td></tr>
  <tr class="alt"><td>GET</td><td><span class="code">/api/payroll/{id}/export</span></td><td>Download one run as CSV</td><td>signed in</td><td>200, 401, 404, 502</td></tr>
  <tr><td>GET</td><td><span class="code">/api/aws/identity</span></td><td>AWS connection status (masked)</td><td>admin</td><td>200, 401, 403, 503</td></tr>
  <tr class="alt"><td>GET</td><td><span class="code">/api/employee-images</span></td><td>Map of employee id to signed photo link</td><td>signed in</td><td>200, 401, 503</td></tr>
  <tr><td>PUT</td><td><span class="code">/api/employee-images/{employeeId}</span></td><td>Upload or replace a photo</td><td>admin</td><td>200, 400, 401, 403, 404, 413, 502, 503</td></tr>
  <tr class="alt"><td>DELETE</td><td><span class="code">/api/employee-images/{employeeId}</span></td><td>Delete a photo</td><td>admin</td><td>204, 400, 401, 403, 503</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>ai-service (port 8000)</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th style="width:12%">Method</th><th style="width:30%">Path</th><th>Purpose</th><th style="width:12%">Access</th><th style="width:20%">Responses</th></tr>
  <tr><td>GET</td><td><span class="code">/health</span></td><td>Liveness; <span class="code">mode</span> is <i>openai</i> or <i>rules-only</i></td><td>open</td><td>200</td></tr>
  <tr class="alt"><td>POST</td><td><span class="code">/api/ai/analyze</span></td><td>Review a list of payroll records</td><td>signed in</td><td>200, 400, 401, 422, 502</td></tr>
  <tr><td>POST</td><td><span class="code">/api/ai/chat</span></td><td>Ask a question about employees and payroll</td><td>signed in</td><td>200, 400, 401, 422, 502, 503</td></tr>
</table>

